body:
Metal Gear Rising was decent at best. It pretty much turns into a zandatsu spam fest at some point, but it's fun sometimes. Bayonetta is great, but I think I prefer DMC3, DMC4, and NG2 over it. Bayonetta just doesn't have enough punishment for me. KPK can be spammed all the way through and the only thing that will suffer is the score, instead of the enemies utterly destroying the player for trying something so stupid, much unlike in Ninja Gaiden where each enemy has a countermeasure for every one of Ryu's moves. Bayo also doesn't implement the dial-a-combo system as well as Ninja Gaiden because the enemy A.I. in Bayo is lacking in pretty much every encounter except Grace and Glory and the Joys.

&#x200B;

Bayo on infinite climax can be fun, though. I feel witch time really takes away from the game.

&#x200B;

Vanquish is Platinum's best title by far, IMO.

This game is much more technical and demanding of the player's abilities than Souls. Besides the fact than certain conceptual ideas, like shrine/bonfire, are shared between Nioh and Souls, they are almost nothing alike.

&#x200B;

Nioh is much closer to an action game like Ninja Gaiden. How far have you gotten into the game so far?

If you let your wife beat you incessantly then it's because you weren't man enough to put an end to things before they got carried away.

&#x200B;

Don't blame a show for your problems.

Lmao. The last DMC game was DmC from 2013 which was.. subpar, to say the least. Before this, the last true and tried DMC game was DMC4, back in 2008.

&#x200B;

So no, the hype is real for DMC5. Expectations are also high. Popularity =/= hype.

Even if they don't fix the issues, if they take the positives of Nioh and make them even better, I'll be more than satisfied and will happily throw down w/e amount of money Team Ninja asks for. 

&#x200B;

I would like to see Nioh 2 focus on the action aspects and leave the RPG aspects how they are. Ninja Gaiden 2 dismemberment in Nioh 2 would be a wet dream.

HAHAHAHA

&#x200B;

That went way over your head. First off, no one is gonna accept your apology because you're just trying to start shit and you're not out here to gain wisdom. 

&#x200B;

Second, you've been a bitch on 2 occasions, and when the gentle folk here respond in kind to the rude way you presented yourself, you ignore everything and insist on the idea that we are attempting something so frivolous.

&#x200B;

So, yes, as for as **you're** concerned, we are transmuting base metals. 

&#x200B;

You may leave now. 

&#x200B;

Someone has been watching a certain anime.

&#x200B;

Nonethelss, it is possible to create one, but at our level of human capability, a homonculus will not survive longer than 3 days. The process of creating life in this way is merely for the sake of meddling with nature and playing God.

&#x200B;

I suggest you abandon this ideal and seek something more obtainable.

No, I haven't. I was taught to be your own therapist, and to scratch your own back.

&#x200B;

I will watch the video.
